#! ia 1.0

@lane authority
  meaning
    says "The authority lane — where governance and authority-facet contracts land: the rules and bindings that say what must hold. Derived from @kind governance and @kind contract (authority facet)."
    answers "Does this node lower into the authority lane?"
  data
    order 0

@lane contracts
  meaning
    says "The contracts lane — where non-authority contracts land: the agreed shapes and interfaces records fill. Derived from @kind contract (non-authority facet)."
    answers "Does this node lower into the contracts lane?"
  data
    order 1

@lane definitions
  meaning
    says "The definitions lane — where definitional nodes land: the declarations of what things ARE. Derived from @kind definition."
    answers "Does this node lower into the definitions lane?"
  data
    order 2

@lane templates
  meaning
    says "The templates lane — where reusable scaffolds land: the parameterized shapes instantiated into concrete records. Derived from @kind template."
    answers "Does this node lower into the templates lane?"
  data
    order 3

@lane enforcement
  meaning
    says "The enforcement lane — where gates and access rules land: the checks and policies evaluated at a crossing. Derived from @kind check and @kind policy."
    answers "Does this node lower into the enforcement lane?"
  data
    order 4

@lane bindings
  meaning
    says "The bindings lane — where wirings land: the projection edges that materialize a record into a host, store, or hook. Derived from @kind binding."
    answers "Does this node lower into the bindings lane?"
  data
    order 5

